# Learning Notes – Sprint 30

## Overview

Sprint 30 focused on creating a reusable Empty State component and using it in the Eligible Jobs component.

## Concepts Learned

- Learned how to create a reusable Lightning Web Component.
- Learned how to use `@api` properties to pass information from a parent component to a child component.
- Understood how a child component can receive a dynamic title and message.
- Learned how to conditionally display an optional action button.
- Understood why meaningful empty states are better than simple "No records found" messages.
- Learned how reusable components can reduce duplicate UI code.
- Understood that reusable components should represent a meaningful business or UI capability.

## Key Takeaways

- Reusable components help reduce code duplication.
- `@api` properties allow parent components to provide data to child components.
- Empty states should clearly explain what is happening to the user.
- A reusable component can be used by multiple components in the application.
- Component reuse should provide meaningful functionality instead of unnecessary abstraction.
- The `EmptyState` component can be reused in future features such as My Applications.
